    "title": "Tickets now on sale for Badlands Circuit Finals Rodeo - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jack Meyer ,\n1 hours ago\nMINOT, ND ( KXNET ) — After months of grueling rodeos across the Midwest, it’s all coming down to one final showdown at the Badlands Circuit Finals this October.\nTickets are now on sale for the Circuit Finals rodeo, which features the top twelve cowboys and cowgirls in each of the eight main event categories across North and South Dakota. Rodeo organizers say that while the finals may still be over a month away, this is a show you don’t want to miss.\nTrinity Health hosts Senior Safari at Roosevelt Park Zoo “It’s the Super Bowl of rodeo for North and South Dakota,” rodeo general manager Max Weppler said. “It’s the best of the best. The best cowboys, cowgirls, the best bucking horses and bulls, the best contract personnel, stock contractors, clowns, announcers — We strive ourselves on having the very best here.”\nGeneral admission tickets start at $25 per person, while children between the ages of 2-12 get in for half that price. Reserved seating starts at $35 per attendee.\nClose Thanks for signing up!\nWatch for us in your inbox.\nSubscribe Now\nToday's Top Stories Copyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KX NEWS.",
